## 2. Experience in one paragraph

Build-3 opens from `index.html` and I could play it from the title to the end: 1-1 → flagpole → castle, then 1-2 (above-ground walk-in, pipe into the underground, brick/`?` rows, piranha pipes, coin-room pipe, exit pipe, flagpole), 1-3 (treetops, four lifts, Paratroopas, midway checkpoint, flagpole and a tall castle), 1-4 (firebars, lava pits, Bowser on the bridge, axe, Toad) and the "YOU CLEARED WORLD 1" screen — on **three lives, no death, final score 066200**, with lives, coins and score carried across all three level changes and the same result in Chromium (manual and real time) and Firefox. Everything I measured in build-2 behaves the same (7 of the 13 regression result files are identical to build-2's; the other 6 differ only where the game was changed on purpose or by timing noise, see row 1–29). The two build-2 minors I was asked to look at are fixed (N1 mute/music, D3 sub-frame key tap). The warp zone works and its three pipes can all be entered, but each ends on a "WARP TO WORLD n / WORLDS 2-8 ARE NOT IN THIS VERSION YET" screen because those worlds do not exist. I found **no blocker**. The most serious problem is in 1-3: the vertical lift **stops carrying Mario once it rises faster than about 1 px/frame, and he sinks through it** (usually into the pit); it can be avoided by boarding on the way down and jumping off, which is what the natural run did. The most visible problem is graphical: **every Koopa, Paratroopa and Bowser is drawn facing the way it came from**, and this has been so since build-1 (I missed it in my two earlier reports; the artist reported it independently as `game-developer#10`).

